From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: quote the settings path

OT_POSIX_SETTINGS_PATH goes into the definition as it is, so the
compiler gets a bare path unless the caller adds quotes, which do not
survive make and the shell.  Add the quotes here.

Upstream: not sent
---
diff --git a/etc/cmake/options.cmake b/etc/cmake/options.cmake
--- a/etc/cmake/options.cmake
+++ b/etc/cmake/options.cmake
@@ -381,7 +381,7 @@
 endif()
 
 if(OT_POSIX_SETTINGS_PATH)
-    target_compile_definitions(ot-config INTERFACE "OPENTHREAD_CONFIG_POSIX_SETTINGS_PATH=${OT_POSIX_SETTINGS_PATH}")
+    target_compile_definitions(ot-config INTERFACE "OPENTHREAD_CONFIG_POSIX_SETTINGS_PATH=\"${OT_POSIX_SETTINGS_PATH}\"")
 endif()
 
 #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
